            "decimals": 1,
            "label": "Overlap",
            "note": "The share of talking time where both people speak at once. Almost none usually means echo cancellation gated one microphone, which erases the very thing a full-duplex model needs to learn. Below 3 percent we flag the conversation.\n\nWe cut both tracks into 20 millisecond frames. A frame counts as speech when it passes three times that track’s own noise floor, or a fixed floor of 0.004, whichever is higher. The figure is the frames where both speak, divided by the frames where either does.",
            "p5": 2.8,
            "p50": 8.3,
            "p95": 20.9,
            "unit": "% of voiced time"
          },
          {
            "binMax": 1440,
